      "used_by": ["α-Reachable Graphs (ICML 2025)"],
      "could_be_applied_to": "Use the quasimetric constant k as a complexity parameter in expressiveness bounds: as k grows, Chamfer becomes 'more metric-like' (quasimetric constant worsens), but expressiveness increases. Characterizing this tradeoff — the price of expressiveness in metric structure — would connect our expressiveness theory to computational search efficiency."
